course: dictionary
lesson: 766
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word beam is a good example. «A beam bridge rests on supports» is about a long, strong piece of wood or metal that holds something up. «Reflective material sends a car's headlight beam back towards the driver» is about a line of light.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the whole sentence and ask: what is the writer talking about? Then try your meaning in the sentence. In «The Badger beams — that's exactly what he thinks!», beams is an action, so it means smiles widely and happily. A line of light would make no sense there.
explain: Check whether beam is a thing or an action. As a noun it is a thing, such as a roof beam or a torch beam. As a verb it is something you do: beam, beams, beamed, beaming. Look at the small words around it, like «a» or «she beamed», to spot which one you have.
fact: A beam can be a long, strong piece of wood or metal that holds up a roof or floor.
fact: A beam can also be a line of light, like the beam from a torch.
fact: To beam means to smile very widely and happily.
fact: A balance beam is a narrow bar that gymnasts walk and jump on.
fact: To beam something means to send it, like a signal or a picture.
exercise: Which meaning of beam fits «A beam bridge rests on supports»? | A line of light | A signal sent through the air | A smile | *A long, strong piece of wood or metal that holds something up
exercise: «Reflective material sends a car's headlight beam back towards the driver.» What does beam mean here? | A wooden bar holding up a roof | To smile widely | *A line of light | A balance bar for gymnasts
exercise: Which sentence uses beam to mean smile widely and happily? | *«When she opened her present, she beamed.» | «The gymnast walked along the beam.» | «The lighthouse beam swept across the sea.» | «The roof beam cracked in the storm.»
test: Gymnasts practise on the balance beam. What is a balance beam? | A long wooden roof support | *A narrow bar that gymnasts walk and jump on | To send a picture through the air | A line of light
test: Ravi asks the class to beam a picture onto the screen. What does beam mean here? | A strong piece of wood | A ray of sunshine through the window | *To send something, like a picture | To smile widely
exam: Read «The children beamed with pride when the teacher praised their picture.» What does beamed mean? | *Smiled very widely and happily | Shone a torch into the dark | Lifted a heavy wooden beam | Sent out a signal
